\f2\b \cf0 Class
\f1\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3 \cf0 \uc0\u9888 \u65039 
\f1  Part of the 
\f2\b classification scheme
\f1\b0  \'97 carries 
\f2\b retention & disposal rules
\f1\b0 . Records get assigned to a class for lifecycle purposes.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This is 
\f2\b NOT
\f1\b0  M-Files' "Class." In M-Files, 
\f0\i Class
\f1\i0  means object-type sub-typing (Contract, Invoice\'85). MoReq's Class \uc0\u8776  M-Files 
\f2\b workflow + retention/disposal logic + a value-list value
\f1\b0 , not the M-Files Class field.\cell \row

