\f2\b \cf0 Service
\f1\b0 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The functional modules (Entity, Classification, Disposal Scheduling, Disposal Holding, Role, Search, Export\'85) that reference each other.\cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 M-Files 
\f2\b features/subsystems
\f1\b0 : permissions (NACLs), workflows, value lists, vault structure, retention policies, search, export. No 1:1 module boundary.\cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec2 The one that will bite you on a vendor requirements sheet is 
\f2\b Class
\f1\b0 . When MoReq2010 (or a records-manager writing to it) says "class," they almost always mean 
\f0\i the retention/disposal classification
\f1\i0 , not M-Files object classes. So a requirement like "records inherit disposal rules from their class" maps to 
\f2\b M-Files workflows + retention policies
\f1\b0 , and answering it against the M-Files 
\f0\i Class
\f1\i0  field would be wrong.\
Two more worth calling out for your yes/no assessment:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Aggregation
\f1\b0  is the biggest conceptual gap. M-Files is metadata/relationship-driven, not folder-driven, so "open/close an aggregation," "child aggregations," and "destroy a closed aggregation" all have to be modelled with 
\f2\b container objects + workflow states + relationships
\f1\b0 , not literal folders. It's 
\f0\i doable
\f1\i0  but it's a design decision, not an out-of-the-box control \'97 worth phrasing carefully rather than a flat "yes."\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Record
\f1\b0  as an immutable declared entity relies on M-Files 
\f2\b workflow state locking + version history
\f1\b0 ; M-Files doesn't have a formal "declare as record" button unless you're on a records-management configuration or add-on.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
